  - id: faith_without_works
    displayName: Faith Without Works Is Dead
    flavorText: James argues that faith without works is dead, pointing to Abraham's
      offering of Isaac and Rahab's reception of the spies as proof that faith and
      works operate together.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Faith without works is dead and cannot save, illustrated by Abraham's
      offering of Isaac and Rahab's reception of the spies, both justified by works.
    deliveredByManagerId: james_brother_of_jesus
    managerId: faith_without_works
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
